 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374965} {:answer/id #uuid "4af7592a-53ab-5029-84a6-0c1ae6f1ecbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eee95f49-2834-5278-87a5-01508ddf4e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374964} :answer-field/id #uuid "e512a023-e97d-55f4-aa03-d4567a201479" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "261b9603-2ac4-5d0d-8b8b-1dfa9f08009a" :question/math-academy-id "q-337936" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=x{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}_{2}={e}^{-x}.$ \n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}={u}_{1}(x),{u}_{2}={u}_{2}(x),$ that satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following constraint equation relating ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a second-order linear inhomogeneous differential equation, the variation of parameters method requires that we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}(x)+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}(x)\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}.\n$$\n\nHere, ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly independent solutions of the corresponding homogeneous equation, and ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nIn this case, we're told that the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={e}^{2x},\\,{y}_{2}={e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our expression for ${y}_{p},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}={u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-x})^{′}.\n$$\n\nWe can form a constraint that relates ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}$ by differentiating ${y}_{p}$ and equating this expression to our constraint on ${y}_{p}^{′}.$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x$ using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ={({u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({u}_{1}{e}^{2x})}^{′}+{({u}_{2}{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-x})^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we equate our two expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x} & ={u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-x})^{′} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x} & =2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}-{u}_{2}{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+\\cancel{2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}-\\cancel{{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}} & =\\cancel{2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}}-\\cancel{{u}_{2}{e}^{-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich finally gives\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-x}=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0d4530-bf50-526c-a975-941ee1fed9a0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a VOP Equation Using the Derivative Constraint"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ebcfc9-08a7-5b03-9884-e85211d1bf24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308760} {:answer/id #uuid "c036d500-b4e2-57b9-ac27-2cc85f7efd56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310299} {:answer/id #uuid "f70b25e6-cb77-5b4c-9d92-0312046ca101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ebcfc9-08a7-5b03-9884-e85211d1bf24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308760} :answer-field/id #uuid "004fd509-8ff5-573f-a9b1-20f9697dd71f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e4b095f-bbca-5f0a-b1c8-c6ee80fe065e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309098} {:answer/id #uuid "35c03ef8-e6d3-5cd6-ade0-bee30d8d222b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309156} {:answer/id #uuid "89357217-a783-5964-99f7-7768c0bf6257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860